Title: I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT A SPEC WAS
Author: vibecode-blog pipeline
Contact: @lazy_genius2025

== act: hook ==

INT. SNOWY CABIN - DAY

A CLAY CHARACTER sits with a single laptop. Beyond the window, three distant towers glow blue in perfect synchronization.

NARRATOR
(cool)
My three computers finally act like one. I can work from anywhere.

Character clicks a key. All screens pulse.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
But getting here? It took six months of absolute hell.

== act: fury ==

INT. DARK OFFICE - NIGHT

Character is buried in red clay wires. Monitor strobes "CRITICAL FAILURE".

NARRATOR
(pissed)
Monday morning. Everything stopped. Ten thousand lines of code, and half of it was garbage.

CLOSE UP - MONITOR

Screen cracks. A door handle labeled "SHELL INJECTION" emerges.

NARRATOR
(raw)
AI wrote a back door. I approved it. I didn't even know it was there.

== act: mess ==

INT. CODE JUNGLE - DAY

Character hacks through duplicating clay vines. 5 robots build 5 conflicting bridges.

NARRATOR
(manic)
Five agents building the same thing. Three date formatters. Four ways to validate a string.

Character pulls a vine. Forest collapses into a clay knot.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
It looked convincing. That's why it was dangerous. I was vibe coding with no map.

== act: insight ==

INT. CLEAN STUDIO - DAY

Character pins a 4-line blueprint to a pristine wall.

NARRATOR
(resolute)
Implementation is free. But deciding what to build? That's the only thing that isn't.

WIDE SHOT

Character walks across a sturdy clay bridge over an organized grid.

NARRATOR
(philosopher)
Specs don't come from conference rooms. They come from the grind.
